#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:10
msgid ""
"NextSync is an independent, unofficial third-party project. It is not "
"affiliated with, sponsored by, endorsed by, maintained by, or otherwise "
"connected to Nextcloud GmbH. Nextcloud is a registered trademark of "
"Nextcloud GmbH.\n"
"\n"
"Bidirectional synchronization can upload, download, replace, conflict, or "
"delete files on both the computer and the configured server. Use this "
"software entirely at your own risk, test it with non-critical data, and "
"maintain independent, restorable backups. The authors and contributors are "
"not responsible for lost, corrupted, deleted, or otherwise damaged data.\n"
"\n"
"The application delegates file reconciliation and conflict handling to "
"nextcloudcmd. Availability of notify_push and other server features depends "
"on the Nextcloud installation. This release was tested with Nextcloud Hub 26 "
"Spring (34.0.1) on Nextcloud AIO. Compatibility with other or future "
"Nextcloud versions is not guaranteed.\n"
"\n"
"No telemetry, advertising, or usage tracking is included. Credentials are "
"stored through the desktop Secret Service. Use of this software is also "
"subject to the GNU General Public License version 3 or later and its "
"warranty disclaimer."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:34
msgid "Version 0.2.0"
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:36
msgid ""
"Each account can now hold several sync folders instead of one: every folder "
"maps a local root to an optional remote path and runs its own "
"synchronization, filesystem watch, deletion guard, exclusions, and "
"nextcloudcmd invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:37
msgid ""
"The setup wizard lets you finish the login without choosing any folder, and "
"folders can be added or removed later from Settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:38
msgid "The account view lists every sync folder of the active account."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:42 src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:226
msgid "Version 0.1.0"
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:44
msgid ""
"NextSync is a fork of PyNextCloud-Sync by ehstbr, renamed and versioned "
"independently from 0.1.0 (each release adds +0.1)."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:45
msgid ""
"Thin-wrapper redesign: the bootstrap staging, safety baseline, run markers, "
"and deletion guard are removed. nextcloudcmd now owns synchronization, "
"conflict resolution, and safety."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:46
msgid ""
"The config schema bumps from v4 to v5 and drops the safety fields "
"automatically; leftover staging trees are removed and legacy safety "
"manifests are archived on first run after upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:47
msgid ""
"A first-sync confirmation dialog appears before the initial run when the "
"local folder, the remote folder, or both are empty, probing the remote side "
"with a shallow WebDAV PROPFIND."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:48
msgid ""
"A new view with Recent activity and conflicted copies lists the files "
"nextcloudcmd preserves as '* (Nextcloud conflicted copy <date>).*' with Keep "
"Local, Keep Remote, and Open in Files actions."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:49
msgid ""
"A lightweight deletion guard blocks synchronization before nextcloudcmd "
"starts when a large share of previously known local files disappears, with "
"Keep Paused, Restore from Nextcloud, or Approve These Deletions Once."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:50
msgid ""
"The account view and tray tooltip now show the current file and processed "
"count during a sync, falling back to the state label when the engine emits "
"no per-file output."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:54
msgid "Version 2.1.0"
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:56
msgid ""
"Added an optional Remote Folder field to the setup wizard so an account can "
"mirror a specific Nextcloud folder instead of the entire account root."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:57
msgid ""
"When a remote folder is configured, the --path argument is passed to "
"nextcloudcmd; leaving the field as / keeps the previous root-to-root "
"behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:58
msgid ""
"Existing configurations migrate transparently to schema version 4 with the "
"remote path defaulting to the account root."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:59
msgid ""
"Two accounts against the same server, user, and local folder but different "
"remote folders are now treated as distinct accounts."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:63
msgid "Version 2.0.0"
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:65
msgid ""
"Added support for multiple Nextcloud accounts, each with its own "
"synchronization, safety, and runtime settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:66
msgid ""
"Existing single-account configurations are migrated automatically on first "
"launch."
msgstr ""

#: src/nextsync/ui/about_content.py:67
msgid ""
"The main window now has an accounts sidebar and a per-account status and "
"activity panel."
